<%# locals: section_id, name, image_id, image_html_name, image_value,
    checkbox_id, checkbox_html_name, show_checkbox -- an attachment's
    preview, its file input and a "Remove image" checkbox (cs-studio spec
    §5.1), wrapped in one `id="<%= section_id %>"` element so a single Turbo
    Stream `replace` can bring all three back in sync with the record after
    a save that touched the attachment (`Admin::SettingsController
    #logo_field_stream`) -- rendered from this one partial on the initial
    GET (`Admin::SettingsFormComponent`) and again from that stream, so
    there is exactly one "what does this section look like right now"
    template.
    `show_checkbox` is always the record's *current* `attached?`, not "was
    this section just touched" -- an unattached record has nothing to
    remove either way.

    Only the site logo uses this since media library Task 8: a page's hero
    and an image block's image are library images now, chosen through the
    picker (`Admin::Columns::MediaColumnComponent`), and the logo stays a
    `SiteSetting` attachment of its own (global constraints). %>
<div id="<%= section_id %>">
  <%= render Admin::Columns::ImageColumnComponent.new(name: name, id: image_id, html_name: image_html_name, value: image_value) %>

  <% if show_checkbox %>
    <div class="mb-4 -mt-2">
      <label class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-meta">
        <%= check_box_tag checkbox_html_name, "1", false, id: checkbox_id,
              class: "size-4 rounded-cs border-line-strong text-accent focus:outline-2 focus:outline-accent" %>
        Remove image
      </label>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
